    {
      "number": 2,
      "folder": "02-components",
      "title": "Components",
      "ids": [
        18
      ],
      "objective": "Understand the capabilities that turn a model into a system that can observe, decide and act.",
      "intro": "The components work together: perception supplies observations; memory supplies relevant state; reasoning and planning choose what to do; tools perform actions; communication coordinates handoffs; and feedback supports improvement. These functions can be implemented differently in different systems. Separate the model's learned capabilities from context and persistent stores. Understand what each component contributes before choosing a framework.",
