    {
      "number": 6,
      "folder": "06-multi-agent-systems",
      "title": "Multi-agent systems",
      "ids": [
        56
      ],
      "objective": "Design collaboration around responsibilities, shared evidence and measurable outcomes.",
      "intro": "This chapter revisits subjects that IBM also places under Architecture. The emphasis here is operating a team: clear responsibilities, shared evidence, handoff contracts, conflict resolution and a final artifact owner. Multi-agent collaboration can help with separable work, but it can also amplify errors or add delay. Evaluate it against a simpler workflow before adopting it.",
