      "number": 8,
      "folder": "08-governance",
      "title": "Governance",
      "ids": [
        83
      ],
      "objective": "Define ownership, evaluation, security, supervision and operational accountability.",
      "intro": "Governance defines who owns agents, what they may do and how acceptable performance is demonstrated. Evaluation examines outputs and trajectories; observability helps diagnose behavior; security constrains access and execution; human review resolves consequential decisions. Keep these responsibilities attached to the actual workflow rather than treating them as optional paperwork.",
