    {
      "number": 9,
      "folder": "09-agentic-rag",
      "title": "Agentic RAG",
      "ids": [
        92
      ],
      "objective": "Retrieve the right evidence, assess its quality, and answer within what it supports.",
      "intro": "RAG supplies evidence from external documents instead of relying only on a model's trained knowledge. Agentic RAG decides how to retrieve, whether the evidence is sufficient and whether another step is justified. Chunking affects what can be retrieved; corrective retrieval handles weak results. Citation quality, source applicability and honest limits matter more than the number of retrieved passages.",
